# A keyed read that names every field.
#
# Should: be refused by `kanso check`, pointing at shape/shape.kso:9. The
# rule is a compile-time rule elsewhere: in the todo port,
# `{ items next_id } = st` was refused when checked, though with the
# message "unknown name `next_id`".
#
# Does: `kanso check main.kso` says ok. Running it, on both engines, stops
# with
#   error[runtime]: a keyed read omits at least one field; reading every
#   field is the positional form
# and no location at all. In the port the same error carried a location
# naming the calling module and no file (`--> todo:26:29` for a read at
# http/response.kso:26).
import "./shape"

p = shape/make 1 2
print "{shape/swapped p}"
